# Round 16 — THE PUBLIC PAD. Per-lane .gitignore files cover each lane's fetched corpora
# (P1 blockchair dumps, P2 beacon/random.org archives, P3 RAND + Cicada pads); this block
# covers the shared instrument and lane P0, which fetches nothing.
#
# REGENERATION
#   trigram_idx.npy      — the rune-index trigram model, rebuilt automatically on first
#                          call to lib_padsweep.trigram_model() from liber-primus/data/
#                          {kjv,moby,pride,war}.txt. Deleting it costs one rebuild.
#   P0_dense/ckpt*/      — per-config sweep checkpoints, one JSON per (pad, builder, sign).
#                          Rebuild:  python P0_dense/sweep.py     (resumable — it skips any
#                          config that already has a checkpoint), then P0_dense/merge.py
#                          re-collects them into results*.json.
#   *.log / *.out / *.err — raw stdout of long sweeps. The numbers that matter are copied
#                          into results*.json and RESULTS.md.
#
# COMMITTED (the record of what was tried, self-sufficient without any of the above):
#   lib_padsweep.py, PREREG.md, SYNTHESIS.md, each lane's scripts, results*.json, RESULTS.md
trigram_idx.npy
